This project has a graphify knowledge graph at graphify-out/.

**Windows SAC:** never `graphify.exe`. Use signed Python: `py -3.12 -m graphify …` (or `scripts\Harden-GraphifyShim.ps1` in DABOS so bare `graphify` → `.cmd`).

- For codebase or architecture questions, when `graphify-out/graph.json` exists, first run `py -3.12 -m graphify query "<question>"` (or `path` / `explain`). These return a scoped subgraph, usually much smaller than `GRAPH_REPORT.md` or raw grep output.
- If graphify-out/wiki/index.md exists, navigate it instead of reading raw files
- Read graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md only for broad architecture review or when query/path/explain do not surface enough context
- After modifying code files in this session, run `py -3.12 -m graphify update .` to keep the graph current (AST-only, no API cost)
